{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause evidence (AC1), from Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744) and a local run of the 133 tests under `PYTHONWARNDEFAULTENCODING=1 -W always::EncodingWarning`:\n\n1. `hatch_build.py:112` writes the generated `src/rebar/_build_info.py` without `encoding`, so on Windows its docstring em dash is cp1252 byte `0x97`. Every UTF-8 whole-tree scan (`tests/_tree_scan.py:40`, `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:320`, wheel/sdist checks) then fails `UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0x97 in position 45` — the traceback shows `input = b'\"\"\"Generated at build time by hatch_build.py \\x97 do NOT edit...'`. This one defect accounts for most of the 133.\n2. `rebar explain plan` exits 1 with `UnicodeEncodeError: 'charmap' codec can't encode characters` (stdout is cp1252 when piped).\n3. `binding_repository.py:76` writes `{\\r\\n ...` (no `newline`), failing 6 byte-exact tests.\n4. Test-side locale-default reads (`'charmap' codec can't decode byte 0x90/0x8f/0x9d`), a text-mode CRLF expected-bytes fixture in `test_complexity_baseline.py:493`, and a pytester child decoded as UTF-8 in `test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py`.\n\nLint rule decision: PLW1514 is preview-only in ruff 0.16.3, and it does not flag `hatch_build.py:112` (Path receiver not inferred) or `subprocess(..., text=True)`, so it would not have caught root cause 1; not adopted. Plan-review rounds added: the CLI-output consumers (reconfiguring stdout to UTF-8 requires parents to decode UTF-8), `hatch_build.py:45` and `reclaim_dry_run.py:239`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795029822288972976,"uuid":"2e7225c1-7510-4a1c-8ff4-9eb85e0e4cd2"}